Version 0.108
-------------

	o SaveFile uses XferInfo structure instead of ExNexting
	through the directory looking for new files.

Version 0.109
-------------

	o Because of our new esteemed beta-tester, Martin Ogden who
        has over 28,000 files, I decided to re-write most of the
        file handling routines to a new method worthy of such
        a huge file base.
        o First thing was to knock out the internal memory indexing,
        which was fairly fast, but a pain in the neck to load, and
	it fragmented the memory no end.
        o The file bases are now indexed as follows (to the Pipeline
        File Directory)
                o FileDesc.AreaNumber -- Records the File Descriptions
                o FileData.AreaNumber -- Records the File Data.
                o A-INDEX
                o B-INDEX
                o C-INDEX
                   .. ..
                   .. ..
                o #-INDEX -- alphabetical index files.
                o FilePointers -- For recording of the alphabetical
                  highs and lows of each area.
                o FileIndex -- File Offsets for each Number->Header Offset
	o As you may have guessed, the previous file format is by
        no means compatible with the previous.
        o There are two new programs.
           o BulkUploader -- Uploads files using their comment field,
             or a specially formatted text file.
           o DumpFileList -- Dumps the old format files into a text
             file which can be loaded in by BulkUploader.
	o Every internal structure relating to the files have been
	changed, and more structures have been added.
	o See pipeutil.fd for new library functions.
	o Please re-compile, and in some cases re-code any programs
        that use the pipeline file functions.

